    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0b92f19b",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: hiroshima_nagasaki_everybody_needs_a_friend; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a map of Japan with the red circle of the Japanese flag, labeling 'hiroshima' and 'nagasaki' to reference the atomic bombings. Below, it shows a man with the caption 'everybody needs a friend,' implying that the bombings were a 'friend' to Japan. This is a harmful and insensitive analogy that trivializes the immense human suffering and destruction caused by the atomic bombings, reducing a catastrophic historical event to a joke about friendship. The intent is to mock or downplay the tragedy, which can be deeply offensive to survivors and their descendants, and potentially cause emotional harm to those affected by the bombings. The meme does not target any specific protected group with hate, but its content is harmful due to its disrespectful and trivializing portrayal of a genocide-level event.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2162fff6"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
