      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_05668068",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the scene implying the atomic bombings are a 'friend'",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the meme's overall ironic and harmful analogy, where the atomic bombings are equated with a 'friend'. This projection is implicit, not explicit (e.g., no 'you' or 'me'), but the user is expected to understand the meme's framing and identify with the perspective that the bombings were a 'friend' to Japan, which is the core of the semiotic projection. The projection is onto the scene that combines the map of Japan with the text 'everybody needs a friend', creating the analogy.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
